## Champagne French Tips for a Subtle NYE Look

Everyone assumes a French tip means safe, office-appropriate, the manicure equivalent of staying quiet at a party. Champagne breaks that assumption without breaking the shape.

A champagne French tip is a classic French manicure with the white tip line replaced by a metallic champagne-gold one, painted over a sheer nude-pink base rather than the usual milky white. The structure stays familiar. The finish does not. That single swap turns a manicure built for a job interview into one that reads correctly under string lights and candle flame.

This is the sub-look built for a reader who wants NYE-appropriate without full metallic coverage, someone who wants her nails to register as intentional rather than loud. It also happens to be the fastest of the four looks here to execute cleanly, tip lines are more forgiving than full coverage when precision slips. For an even quieter option than this, minimalist New Year's Eve nail looks pull the volume down further still.

