## Does Champagne Work on Every Skin Tone?

Yes, champagne works across every skin tone, because the shade itself shifts depending on what it is paired against rather than staying fixed. That adaptability is exactly what makes it different from a color like true silver or straight white gold, which tend to flatter a narrower range.

On fair skin, champagne reads close to its purest form, pale, pink-toned, quietly metallic. On medium and olive skin, the same polish shifts warmer, picking up more gold and less pink, which reads as richer rather than washed out. On deep skin tones, champagne turns genuinely luminous, the shimmer catching more visibly against a deeper base and producing more contrast than it does on lighter skin, not less.

The undertone question matters more than the depth of the skin tone itself. A cooler-toned champagne, more pink than gold, tends to sit best on cool undertones, while a warmer, more gold-forward champagne reads better against warm undertones. Testing a swatch against the inner wrist before committing settles this faster than any general rule can.

