## How to DIY Champagne Chrome Nails at Home

Champagne chrome nails at home start with a gel base coat and a sheer pink or nude gel color, cured under a lamp, then a thin layer of champagne chrome powder buffed in with a silicone applicator before sealing with a no-wipe top coat. It is one of the most DIY-friendly versions of <strong>champagne nails new years</strong> looks, and the whole process takes under an hour once the products are on hand.

Start with clean, shaped nails and a light buff to remove shine from the natural nail. Apply the gel base coat and cure. Follow with one or two thin coats of the sheer pink or nude gel, curing between coats, since chrome powder needs a slightly tacky surface to grip. Dip the silicone applicator into the chrome powder and buff it across the nail in small circular motions until the shimmer builds evenly, then seal everything under a no-wipe top coat and cure a final time.

The most common mistake is applying the chrome powder to a fully cured, glossy top coat instead of the tacky gel layer underneath. Powder will not grip a slick surface no matter how much product goes on, so timing that step correctly matters more than the brand of powder used.

